dialog show @s {type:"minecraft:notice",title:{text:"TMF Changelog",color:"gold",bold:true},body:[{type:"minecraft:plain_message",contents:{text:"TMF v1.11.2 (for Minecraft Java 26.3)\n\nv1.11.2\n• AFK Detection is now off by default.\n• Faster Paths, Fence Jumping and Biome Change Info are now opt-in: each player switches them on in /trigger tmf.\n• Campfire Regen tells you when you step into a campfire's warmth.\n\nv1.11.1\n• New: Campfire Regen.\n• The player menu is split into categories, like the admin panel.\n• Waypoint guiding works (the top bar stayed empty).\n• Campfire Timer groups identical items, e.g. 4× Raw Beef 0:12.\n• Slime Chunk Checker, Waypoints and Compass Coordinates are now off by default.\n\nv1.11.0\n• New: Creeper No-Grief, Ghast No-Grief, No Zombie Door Breaking (new Mob griefing category, together with Enderman Anti-Grief and a switch for the vanilla mob_griefing game rule).\n• New: Pet Health, Animal Owners, Crop Growth Info, Biome Change Info, Campfire Timer, Furnace Progress, Slime Chunk Checker, Arrow Counter, Compass Coordinates, Waypoints, Entity Crowd Warning.\n• New admin tools: Player inspector, Lag helper, Slime chunk seed.\n• Veinminer and Tree Feller: each player picks Off, Sneaking or Always.\n• The Coordinates HUD moved from above the hotbar to a small bar at the top of the screen.\n• New admin category Info & HUD; Movement & info is now Movement.\n\nv1.10.0\n• Admin panel: features are grouped into categories (Mining & tools, Farming & building, Inventory, Pets & mobs, Combat, Movement & info, Multiplayer), each showing how many of its features are on.\n\nv1.9.2\n• Item Magnet is now switched off server-wide by default.\n\nv1.9.1\n• Tree Feller no longer tracks placed logs. It now only fells real trees: the trunk must end in natural leaves (player-placed leaves don't count), and it never spreads more than 7 blocks sideways or below the chopped log.\n\nv1.9.0\n• Renamed to TMF – Too Many Features. Commands are now /trigger tmf, /trigger tmf.stats and /function tmf:admin.\n• Tree Feller no longer cuts logs that players placed (logs placed from this version on).\n\nv1.8.0\n• New: Wandering Trader Alert, Sort Chest, Pickup Notices, Item Magnet, Breeding Info, Sapling Replant, Copper Oxidation Info, Playtime Milestones, Day Counter.\n\nv1.7.0\n• Removed: Armor Stand Editor.\n• Tool Protector, Tool Auto-Swap and the Coordinates HUD are now off for each player until they switch them on in /trigger tmf.\n\nv1.6.0\n• Renamed to AtQ – All the Quality (formerly QoL+).\n\nv1.5.0\n• Tool Auto-Swap also swaps while you keep mining (tunnelling), works up to your full reach then, and also switches away from swords.\n• Features switched off by the server no longer appear in the player menu.\n\nv1.4.0\n• New default selection: only 16 features start switched on (use Presets → Everything on to enable all).\n• Tool Auto-Swap reacts instantly to your first left-click and ignores chests, doors, crafting tables and other blocks you right-click.\n• Coordinates HUD is now light grey. Spawn-Proof Checker shows one small flame per spot.\n• Removed: Hunger HUD.\n\nv1.3.0\n• Renamed: Tool Auto-Swap is now Tool Protector; Best Tool Switcher is now Tool Auto-Swap.\n• Tool Auto-Swap now swaps only when you start breaking a block, not when you just look at it.\n• Spawn-Proof Checker markers are brighter and visible in the dark.\n• Removed: Player Pings, biome in the Coordinates HUD.\n\nv1.2.0\n• New: Veinminer, Tree Feller, Fence Jumping.\n• Ladder Dropping now also places ladders where there is no wall behind them.\n\nv1.1.0\n• New: Right-Click Harvest, Invisible Item Frames, Armor Stand Editor, No Crop Trampling, Fast Leaf Decay, Armor Warning, Best Tool Switcher, Coordinates HUD, Spawn-Proof Checker, Player Pings.\n• Removed: XP Bottling.\n• Left-clicking a ladder while holding ladders now breaks it.\n\nv1.0.0\n• 20 toggleable features with a player menu (/trigger tmf) and an admin panel.\n• Personal opt-out for player-facing features, admin locks to force them on.\n• Presets: Everything on, Vanilla+, Minimal, All off.\n• Performance mode for busy servers.\n• Clean uninstall from the admin panel.",color:"white"},width:340}],pause:false,action:{label:{text:"Back"},action:{type:"minecraft:run_command",command:"/trigger tmf set 2"}}}
